WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.994 --> 00:00:16.776
his return from Monkey City, Mowgli lived happily among the wolf pack.

2
00:00:17.737 --> 00:00:19.678
He grew taller and stronger.

3
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.181
He hunted and swam.

4
00:00:26.502 --> 00:00:36.071
He sat in the sun, and he ate and slept—then ate and slept again.

5
00:00:38.252 --> 00:00:43.795
At Council Rock the wolves often asked Mowgli to pull sharp thorns from their paws.

6
00:00:46.196 --> 00:00:48.958
Mowgli noticed something strange whenever he did it.

7
00:00:49.938 --> 00:00:53.100
If he stared at the wolves, they quickly looked away.

8
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.542
"That's odd," he thought.

9
00:00:56.562 --> 00:00:59.044
"Are the wolves afraid of me?"

10
00:01:02.628 --> 00:01:05.569
Mowgli sometimes saw Shere Khan in the jungle.

11
00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.711
Mowgli tried to keep his distance.

12
00:01:09.811 --> 00:01:13.753
But many of the young wolves were growing loyal to Shere Khan.

13
00:01:14.753 --> 00:01:17.014
The tiger tossed them scraps of food.

14
00:01:18.375 --> 00:01:19.716
He praised them too.

15
00:01:19.736 --> 00:01:23.657
"What fine, brave hunters you are!"

16
00:01:24.258 --> 00:01:25.538
Shere Khan purred.

17
00:01:25.558 --> 00:01:29.800
"I don't know why you let Akela lead you.

18
00:01:30.592 --> 00:01:32.873
He's getting so old and weak."

19
00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:38.395
"Mowgli might lead the pack one day," a young wolf said.

20
00:01:38.415 --> 00:01:41.216
"The man cub is very smart."

21
00:01:42.217 --> 00:01:46.578
"He can even remove thorns from our paws," another wolf said.

22
00:01:46.598 --> 00:01:49.260
"That man cub again!"

23
00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.020
Shere Khan growled.

24
00:01:51.861 --> 00:01:54.182
"He is no better than any of you!"

25
00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.743
Some of the wolves growled too.

26
00:01:57.763 --> 00:02:00.104
"You're right, Shere Khan.

27
00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:02.421
Mowgli is not even a wolf!"

28
00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:06.582
Bagheera watched what was happening within the wolf pack.

29
00:02:07.543 --> 00:02:09.003
And he didn't like it.

30
00:02:09.023 --> 00:02:15.726
"Mowgli, how many times have I told you that Shere Khan is your enemy?"

31
00:02:16.006 --> 00:02:17.307
he asked one afternoon.

32
00:02:18.407 --> 00:02:21.769
The two friends were lying on some leaves in the warm sun.

33
00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.170
Mowgli laughed.

34
00:02:26.251 --> 00:02:29.092
"As many times as there are nuts on that tree!"

35
00:02:30.176 --> 00:02:31.057
He shook his head.

36
00:02:31.837 --> 00:02:35.039
Bagheera was always giving him warnings and advice.

37
00:02:35.059 --> 00:02:38.721
"Well, listen carefully," Bagheera said.

38
00:02:38.741 --> 00:02:40.962
"Akela is getting old.

39
00:02:41.582 --> 00:02:44.044
Soon he will be too weak to lead the pack.

40
00:02:45.004 --> 00:02:47.265
That's when the younger wolves will take action.

41
00:02:48.506 --> 00:02:50.507
They will try to throw you out of the pack."

42
00:02:52.088 --> 00:02:54.829
"They won't throw me out of the pack!"

43
00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:57.371
Mowgli was still laughing.

44
00:02:57.391 --> 00:02:59.512
"I live in the jungle.

45
00:03:00.132 --> 00:03:01.313
I obey its law.

46
00:03:02.293 --> 00:03:05.975
I even pull thorns from my brothers' and sisters' paws."

47
00:03:05.995 --> 00:03:10.096
"Those things are true," Bagheera said firmly.

48
00:03:10.116 --> 00:03:12.257
"But you're not a wolf.

49
00:03:12.678 --> 00:03:13.398
You're a human.

50
00:03:14.218 --> 00:03:15.879
And someday you will live among them."

51
00:03:17.059 --> 00:03:18.760
"I don't think so, Bagheera."

52
00:03:19.641 --> 00:03:20.541
Mowgli yawned.

53
00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:27.424
I go to the hill to look down at the people's village.

54
00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.621
But I never talk to the villagers.

55
00:03:31.241 --> 00:03:32.621
I don't hunt with them.

56
00:03:33.982 --> 00:03:37.343
Anyway, you've lived in the jungle for your whole life.

57
00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:39.863
You don't know anything about people."

58
00:03:41.264 --> 00:03:43.964
The panther shifted his paws and looked away.

59
00:03:43.984 --> 00:03:47.005
"I'm sorry to say this," he said.

60
00:03:47.025 --> 00:03:49.526
"But most of the wolves hate you.

61
00:03:50.866 --> 00:03:53.307
They think you're wiser and stronger than they are.

62
00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.328
That's why they look away when you stare at them.

63
00:03:57.416 --> 00:03:58.377
They are your enemies."

64
00:04:00.118 --> 00:04:05.661
"What?" Mowgli felt stung, as if a bee had landed on his skin.

65
00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:07.602
He leaped up.

66
00:04:07.622 --> 00:04:10.283
"I thought they were my friends!

67
00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.205
Bagheera, what should I do?"

68
00:04:13.225 --> 00:04:17.107
"You must protect yourself," Bagheera said.

69
00:04:17.127 --> 00:04:21.429
"Akela is not going to be able to lead the pack for much longer.

70
00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:25.912
As soon as he fails at hunting, the young wolves will turn against him.

71
00:04:26.848 --> 00:04:30.009
They'll go to Council Rock, and—I've got it!"

72
00:04:30.589 --> 00:04:31.689
Bagheera smiled.

73
00:04:31.709 --> 00:04:35.850
"You must go down to the humans' village in the valley.

74
00:04:36.571 --> 00:04:39.211
Get some of the red flower, which they grow there."

75
00:04:40.572 --> 00:04:41.972
"The red flower?"

76
00:04:42.652 --> 00:04:43.612
Mowgli repeated.

77
00:04:45.013 --> 00:04:48.814
Every beast in the jungle lived in fear of the humans' fire.

78
00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:53.495
"The red flower grows outside their huts at twilight.

79
00:04:54.275 --> 00:04:55.596
I could try to get some."

80
00:04:55.616 --> 00:04:57.842
"Good!" Bagheera nodded.
